"""
=============================================================================
 RAG Vector Store — standalone prototype (zero external dependencies)
=============================================================================

WHAT THIS IS
------------
A self-contained RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) pipeline you can run
and test on its own, BEFORE it is wired into main.py's existing
SEED_DOCUMENTS / PassageIndex / decide() structure.

It has three parts:

  1. DUMMY_DOCUMENTS   - synthetic test data, CLEARLY MARKED as fake (see
                          "ABOUT THE DUMMY DATA" below). Structured exactly
                          like main.py's SEED_DOCUMENTS so it is a drop-in
                          fixture for testing the retrieval pipeline without
                          touching real content.
  2. VectorStore       - a small embedding + cosine-similarity index
                          (pure Python, no numpy/no external embedding API).
  3. rag_loop()        - an interactive question-answer loop that ONLY
                          answers using text pulled from retrieved passages.
                          If retrieval confidence is too low, or the corpus
                          doesn't cover the question, it refuses instead of
                          guessing. This is what keeps it from hallucinating.

Run it directly:
    python rag_vector_store.py

No pip installs required — everything here is the standard library.
=============================================================================
"""

